00:00:00,010 --> 00:01:33,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

1
00:01:56,720 --> 00:01:59,561
Pretty ridiculous pose.

2
00:01:59,561 --> 00:02:04,080
But pretty handsome face.

3
00:02:25,080 --> 00:02:27,360
- Morning.
- Morning.

4
00:02:27,360 --> 00:02:30,680
You slept like that all night?

5
00:02:30,680 --> 00:02:35,041
Your carpet is really uncomfortable
to sleep on.

6
00:02:35,041 --> 00:02:36,840
Are you laughing? Still laughing?

7
00:02:36,840 --> 00:02:39,201
Help me up, quick.

8
00:02:39,201 --> 00:02:41,400
If it's so uncomfortable,

9
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:45,321
why didn't you go back to your king-size bed?

10
00:02:45,321 --> 00:02:47,001
- I've got a stiff neck.
- You're quite heavy.

11
00:02:47,001 --> 00:02:48,360
Easy.

12
00:02:48,360 --> 00:02:50,400
My goodness.

13
00:02:50,400 --> 00:02:51,840
Lean on it.

14
00:02:53,041 --> 00:02:54,042
Get up, hurry.

15
00:02:54,042 --> 00:02:56,240
I'm going to go change.

16
00:02:57,080 --> 00:02:58,081
Where are you going?

17
00:02:58,081 --> 00:02:59,120
To the supermarket.

18
00:02:59,120 --> 00:03:00,721
What for?

19
00:03:00,721 --> 00:03:01,800
To buy groceries and cook.

20
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:03,680
Cook?

21
00:03:03,680 --> 00:03:05,321
You know how to cook?

22
00:03:05,321 --> 00:03:07,001
Is that hard?

23
00:03:07,001 --> 00:03:08,881
I can even fly a plane.

24
00:03:08,881 --> 00:03:11,000
Alright, get up now.

25
00:03:12,080 --> 00:03:13,640
You can cook?

26
00:03:15,360 --> 00:03:19,803
If I weren't so stiff-necked,
I'd look up to you.

27
00:03:20,441 --> 00:03:22,240
Can you really cook?

28
00:03:22,240 --> 00:03:24,520
I'm changing. Why are you coming in?

29
00:03:24,520 --> 00:03:26,281
You asked me to wash up, didn't you?

30
00:03:26,281 --> 00:03:30,400
Go wash up at your place. This is my home.

31
00:03:30,400 --> 00:03:32,240
Isn't this my home too?

32
00:03:32,240 --> 00:03:33,840
Get out!

33
00:03:33,840 --> 00:03:36,520
[Episode 16]
[May Our Adventure Be a Safe Journey]

34
00:03:38,800 --> 00:03:40,300
This one?

35
00:03:41,240 --> 00:03:42,680
No.

36
00:03:47,201 --> 00:03:49,680
Then what do you want to buy?

37
00:03:50,281 --> 00:03:52,120
I don't know.

38
00:03:52,840 --> 00:03:56,280
So, what do you want to cook today?

39
00:03:57,600 --> 00:03:59,400
No idea.

40
00:04:01,001 --> 00:04:02,880
What are you looking at?

41
00:04:02,880 --> 00:04:05,280
Keep looking, and I'll eat you up.

42
00:04:06,840 --> 00:04:08,281
Eat me?

43
00:04:08,281 --> 00:04:10,760
How, if I may ask?

44
00:04:10,760 --> 00:04:12,640
Steamed?

45
00:04:12,640 --> 00:04:14,680
Boiled?

46
00:04:14,680 --> 00:04:16,800
Or raw marinated?

47
00:04:16,800 --> 00:04:18,560
Deep-fried.

48
00:04:19,481 --> 00:04:21,280
That ruthless?

49
00:04:25,760 --> 00:04:28,281
What are you looking at?

50
00:04:28,281 --> 00:04:30,680
My girlfriend. She's pretty, isn't she?

51
00:04:31,481 --> 00:04:33,440
Not as pretty as you.

52
00:04:33,440 --> 00:04:35,721
Why the sudden modesty?

53
00:04:35,721 --> 00:04:40,280
If I weren't so modest,
I'd have a ton of boyfriends by now.

54
00:04:55,029 --> 00:04:57,387
What are you doing? Right here?

55
00:04:57,387 --> 00:05:00,346
Can't win the argument, so I'll fight back.

56
00:05:02,721 --> 00:05:07,601
Alright, I'm sorry, my bad.

57
00:05:07,601 --> 00:05:09,921
Listen,

58
00:05:09,921 --> 00:05:14,320
if you ever ignore my texts, get drunk,

59
00:05:14,320 --> 00:05:16,360
and make me wait up late again,

60
00:05:16,360 --> 00:05:19,241
you'll hear from me once in a blue moon.

61
00:05:22,921 --> 00:05:27,200
Thanks, that's better than last time
when you said you'd send me a wreath.

62
00:05:28,120 --> 00:05:29,200
Milk?

63
00:05:29,200 --> 00:05:31,120
No.

64
00:05:31,120 --> 00:05:32,360
You should have some.

65
00:05:32,360 --> 00:05:34,960
- To grow taller.
- Grow taller?

66
00:05:34,960 --> 00:05:36,800
Like I need that.

67
00:06:01,481 --> 00:06:03,000
Here. Put it here.

68
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:04,440
Over here. Set it down.

69
00:06:04,440 --> 00:06:05,880
Right.

70
00:06:05,880 --> 00:06:07,440
- Come on.
- All right.

71
00:06:07,440 --> 00:06:08,481
Put them together.

72
00:06:08,481 --> 00:06:10,181
Okay.

73
00:06:22,440 --> 00:06:25,240
- I'm off.
- That's it?

74
00:06:48,120 --> 00:06:50,281
<i>♪ Time grinds down the brave and strong ♪</i>

75
00:06:50,281 --> 00:06:53,721
<i>♪ Who holds the fort
when the founders are gone? ♪</i>

76
00:06:53,721 --> 00:06:56,041
<i>♪ One sword, one drink, one road I tread ♪</i>

77
00:06:56,041 --> 00:06:58,572
<i>♪ One step from the sky ahead ♪</i>

78
00:06:58,572 --> 00:06:59,961
<i>♪ Whose world? Whose fight? ♪</i>

79
00:06:59,961 --> 00:07:02,880
<i>♪ Three strikes
and I'll blow out your candlelight ♪</i>

80
00:07:06,521 --> 00:07:09,721
My dear "Captain" Ruan,
I've watched this video ten thousand times.

81
00:07:09,721 --> 00:07:11,120
I can't anymore.

82
00:07:11,120 --> 00:07:12,401
Let me do it. You take a break.

83
00:07:12,401 --> 00:07:14,401
No way.

84
00:07:14,401 --> 00:07:16,281
Get back.

85
00:07:16,281 --> 00:07:20,440
I told you,
the kitchen is off-limits to you today.

86
00:07:20,440 --> 00:07:22,181
Go.

87
00:07:23,281 --> 00:07:25,440
Your stage.

88
00:07:25,440 --> 00:07:26,961
Strike a pose.

89
00:07:26,961 --> 00:07:28,801
Keep it up.

90
00:07:31,320 --> 00:07:34,600
Looks good. Let's start with the egg.

91
00:07:38,401 --> 00:07:40,101
How is it?

92
00:07:41,300 --> 00:07:44,500
Really good. Big improvement.

93
00:07:45,401 --> 00:07:47,101
Now try this one.

94
00:07:49,233 --> 00:07:50,933
Is it good?

95
00:07:51,734 --> 00:07:53,601
Looks great, smells great.

96
00:07:53,601 --> 00:07:56,000
The taste is a bit off.

97
00:07:58,081 --> 00:08:00,320
Let me try.

98
00:08:00,320 --> 00:08:03,520
- No, it's too spicy for you.
- I made it.

99
00:08:13,921 --> 00:08:15,161
What did I make?

100
00:08:15,161 --> 00:08:17,601
Told you not to try it.

101
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:23,521
But it is perfect for me.

102
00:08:23,521 --> 00:08:26,120
Everything tastes good
to you study-abroad folks, right?

103
00:08:26,120 --> 00:08:30,240
When you're living on cold food,
anything hot is a win.

104
00:08:30,240 --> 00:08:31,940
Quite nice.

105
00:08:33,080 --> 00:08:35,080
Well, with the Spring Festival rush coming up,

106
00:08:35,080 --> 00:08:39,361
I wanted to make you a proper meal.

107
00:08:39,361 --> 00:08:41,960
Much appreciated, "Captain" Ruan.

108
00:08:41,960 --> 00:08:45,641
Though you almost did me in
before the rush even started.

109
00:08:45,641 --> 00:08:47,921
But you're eating it just fine, aren't you?

110
00:08:47,921 --> 00:08:50,241
Yeah. I'll have some more.

111
00:08:50,241 --> 00:08:52,281
That's enough.

112
00:08:52,281 --> 00:08:54,480
I think I have some instant noodles.

113
00:08:54,480 --> 00:08:57,560
- I'll make you those instead.
- Don't bother. Forget the noodles.

114
00:08:57,560 --> 00:08:59,881
This is good enough for me.

115
00:08:59,881 --> 00:09:02,521
Plus, way more flavor
than instant noodles anyway.

116
00:09:02,521 --> 00:09:04,080
What are you saying?

117
00:09:04,080 --> 00:09:05,800
Is my cooking too heavy?

118
00:09:05,800 --> 00:09:07,241
I didn't say that. Not me.

119
00:09:07,241 --> 00:09:08,480
Why are you in?

120
00:09:08,480 --> 00:09:12,200
I've told you, the kitchen is off-limits.

121
00:09:12,200 --> 00:09:13,440
I'm already out, aren't I?

122
00:09:13,440 --> 00:09:15,161
Nope, out again.

123
00:09:15,161 --> 00:09:17,961
Go out, and I'll finish it.

124
00:09:25,840 --> 00:09:28,201
You know, I don't really have to eat that.

125
00:09:29,680 --> 00:09:33,241
You don't? Aren't you hungry?

126
00:09:45,347 --> 00:09:47,746
Now I'm feeling a bit hungry.

127
00:10:22,899 --> 00:10:24,540
The suspension's been lifted.

128
00:10:24,540 --> 00:10:26,740
Why are you still so cold with me?

129
00:10:28,761 --> 00:10:30,481
I'm leaving.

130
00:10:32,320 --> 00:10:34,201
Well,

131
00:10:35,166 --> 00:10:37,821
my family might be coming
for the Spring Festival,

132
00:10:37,821 --> 00:10:40,161
and I was thinking of having them stay
a few extra days.

133
00:10:40,161 --> 00:10:44,321
Are you asking me
to spend the festival with them?

134
00:10:45,041 --> 00:10:49,881
I'm saying maybe you should find a time soon
to pack up your things.

135
00:10:49,881 --> 00:10:52,000
I don't want them to get the wrong idea.

136
00:10:55,560 --> 00:10:58,640
I don't think I even have much
at your place anyway.

137
00:10:59,281 --> 00:11:00,981
I'm leaving.

138
00:11:35,480 --> 00:11:38,001
People leave traces.

139
00:11:38,001 --> 00:11:40,160
You can't erase all of them, can you?

140
00:11:47,200 --> 00:11:50,161
- Let go.
- I've got it.

141
00:11:50,161 --> 00:11:52,241
You promised you wouldn't walk me in.

142
00:11:52,241 --> 00:11:54,200
Why? Give me a reason.

143
00:11:54,200 --> 00:11:56,960
No reason. Why are you like this?
You never keep your word, do you?

144
00:11:56,960 --> 00:11:59,401
<i>Why does everyone else get to love so boldly?</i>

145
00:11:59,401 --> 00:12:00,960
<i>No hiding, no shame?</i>

146
00:12:00,960 --> 00:12:02,281
Was I wrong?

147
00:12:02,281 --> 00:12:04,361
<i>If I fall in love one day,</i>

148
00:12:04,361 --> 00:12:08,200
<i>I will walk with him out in the open.</i>

149
00:12:08,200 --> 00:12:14,080
<i>I wouldn't want us hiding in the shadows like
it's some dirty secret, especially not him.</i>

150
00:12:14,080 --> 00:12:16,641
Fine. I'm going in.

151
00:12:16,641 --> 00:12:18,080
Go ahead.

152
00:12:18,080 --> 00:12:20,121
Bye.

153
00:12:20,121 --> 00:12:23,400
- At least let me watch you walk in.
- Sure.

154
00:12:49,560 --> 00:12:54,361
It's Chinese New Year's Eve,
and we'll all be working when midnight comes,

155
00:12:54,361 --> 00:12:57,480
so I'll hand these out now.

156
00:12:57,480 --> 00:12:59,883
Happy New Year to everyone,

157
00:12:59,883 --> 00:13:01,720
and may we have a safe journey
at the end of the year.

158
00:13:01,720 --> 00:13:04,361
Happy New Year. Safe journey.

159
00:13:04,361 --> 00:13:06,041
- Red envelope for you!
- Thank you, Captain!

160
00:13:06,041 --> 00:13:08,161
- Happy New Year.
- Thank you, Captain.

161
00:13:08,161 --> 00:13:10,001
- Happy New Year.
- Happy New Year.

162
00:13:10,001 --> 00:13:12,560
- Here, Si Xian.
- Happy New Year.

163
00:13:12,560 --> 00:13:15,600
Alright, let's get ready for boarding.

164
00:13:15,600 --> 00:13:17,300
Got it.

165
00:13:18,281 --> 00:13:19,761
- Red envelope!
- Back to work, everyone.

166
00:13:19,761 --> 00:13:20,800
- Let's go.
- Happy New Year.

167
00:13:20,800 --> 00:13:22,280
Let's go.

168
00:13:37,960 --> 00:13:39,600
I'm off.

169
00:13:50,241 --> 00:13:52,960
- Welcome aboard.
- Welcome aboard.

170
00:13:52,960 --> 00:13:54,001
Please take your seats.

171
00:13:54,001 --> 00:13:56,040
Welcome aboard.

172
00:13:57,480 --> 00:14:00,800
- Hello, let me help you with that.
- Okay, thank you.

173
00:14:00,800 --> 00:14:05,320
Excuse me, you're sitting in
the emergency exit row.

174
00:14:22,641 --> 00:14:24,121
<i>Good evening, passengers.</i>

175
00:14:24,121 --> 00:14:26,480
<i>This is your captain speaking.</i>

176
00:14:26,480 --> 00:14:30,921
<i>Welcome aboard
Hengshi Air Flight 5412 to Jiang City.</i>

177
00:14:30,921 --> 00:14:34,200
<i>Our flight time today is
expected to be two hours and ten minutes,</i>

178
00:14:34,200 --> 00:14:37,001
<i>with a cruising altitude of 8,400 meters.</i>

179
00:14:37,001 --> 00:14:40,121
<i>According to the weather forecast,</i>

180
00:14:40,121 --> 00:14:42,881
<i>there may be light turbulence
along the way due to weather,</i>

181
00:14:42,881 --> 00:14:46,360
<i>so please keep your seat belt fastened
at all times.</i>

182
00:14:48,361 --> 00:14:51,680
<i>Today is Chinese New Year's Eve,
a time for family.</i>

183
00:14:51,680 --> 00:14:55,320
<i>After a year of hard work,
travelers are heading home,</i>

184
00:14:55,320 --> 00:14:57,401
<i>carrying both the year's rewards
and their longing for loved ones.</i>

185
00:14:57,401 --> 00:15:03,960
<i>The past year has seen regrets and solace,
gains and attachments,</i>

186
00:15:03,960 --> 00:15:07,241
<i>but none of that can hold back
the steps leading home,</i>

187
00:15:07,241 --> 00:15:10,881
<i>because the warmth of family will always
wash away the weariness of the journey.</i>

188
00:15:10,881 --> 00:15:15,161
<i>It's my honor to be your captain
and take you home for this reunion.</i>

189
00:15:15,161 --> 00:15:17,840
<i>On behalf of the entire crew,</i>

190
00:15:17,840 --> 00:15:20,600
<i>I wish you and your families
a very happy Chinese New Year.</i>

191
00:15:20,600 --> 00:15:24,480
<i>May the year ahead bring you hope,
free you from worry,</i>

192
00:15:24,480 --> 00:15:26,881
<i>guide you toward the light,
and carry you forward in it.</i>

193
00:15:26,881 --> 00:15:30,520
<i>Stay passionate,
and keep chasing the next adventure.</i>

194
00:15:34,161 --> 00:15:36,121
Mentor, happy Chinese New Year.

195
00:15:36,121 --> 00:15:37,200
Happy Chinese New Year.

196
00:15:37,200 --> 00:15:39,081
Happy Chinese New Year.

197
00:16:08,480 --> 00:16:12,400
[Reunion dinner.]
[Family portrait. Happy Spring Festival!]

198
00:16:40,160 --> 00:16:42,840
[Mom]

199
00:16:45,600 --> 00:16:47,080
Hello, Mom.

200
00:16:47,080 --> 00:16:49,361
Happy Chinese New Year.

201
00:16:49,361 --> 00:16:51,200
<i>Happy Chinese New Year.</i>

202
00:16:52,161 --> 00:16:54,480
<i>But you're not even coming home for it.</i>

203
00:16:54,480 --> 00:16:58,760
<i>Don't forget to send your nephew
a red envelope.</i>

204
00:17:01,600 --> 00:17:03,320
Got it.

205
00:17:48,401 --> 00:17:51,360
- Home.
- Home.

206
00:18:21,601 --> 00:18:22,960
You're up?

207
00:18:22,960 --> 00:18:24,561
Need to wait just a bit longer.

208
00:18:24,561 --> 00:18:26,320
Don't rush.

209
00:18:27,440 --> 00:18:29,760
Sit down and watch some TV.

210
00:18:35,547 --> 00:18:38,051
Sorry to keep you waiting.

211
00:18:39,401 --> 00:18:41,101
Everything's ready.

212
00:18:42,440 --> 00:18:44,280
This reunion dinner is a little different.

213
00:18:44,280 --> 00:18:46,280
I made some home-style dishes.

214
00:18:46,280 --> 00:18:48,280
What do you think? Happy with it?

215
00:18:48,280 --> 00:18:49,980
Happy.

216
00:18:51,841 --> 00:18:53,360
Come on.

217
00:18:53,960 --> 00:18:55,680
As per tradition,

218
00:18:55,680 --> 00:19:00,800
let's have our future Captain Ruan
say a few words.

219
00:19:02,801 --> 00:19:04,321
Go ahead.

220
00:19:04,321 --> 00:19:06,281
This is...

221
00:19:06,960 --> 00:19:09,361
This is my first reunion dinner

222
00:19:11,641 --> 00:19:14,000
since my dad passed.

223
00:19:26,801 --> 00:19:28,601
Happy Chinese New Year.

224
00:19:38,280 --> 00:19:40,240
Happy Chinese New Year.

225
00:19:49,801 --> 00:19:51,601
Have a taste.

226
00:20:05,801 --> 00:20:07,501
Delicious.

227
00:20:09,440 --> 00:20:11,140
Not bad.

228
00:20:17,801 --> 00:20:19,501
She...

229
00:20:20,121 --> 00:20:22,081
What's that actress's name?

230
00:20:22,081 --> 00:20:23,280
She's been really popular lately.

231
00:20:23,280 --> 00:20:24,440
She's called...

232
00:20:24,440 --> 00:20:27,561
- Li...
- Li Zhi Huai.

233
00:20:27,561 --> 00:20:29,161
Right, Li Zhi Huai.

234
00:20:29,161 --> 00:20:30,440
She's huge this year.

235
00:20:30,440 --> 00:20:32,680
I watched one of her shows just the other day.

236
00:20:32,680 --> 00:20:34,601
You know her too?

237
00:20:34,601 --> 00:20:36,640
Then she's really everywhere.

238
00:20:38,040 --> 00:20:40,440
Here, have a dumpling.

239
00:20:41,601 --> 00:20:43,214
Wait.

240
00:20:43,214 --> 00:20:45,533
Before we eat the dumplings,

241
00:20:46,960 --> 00:20:48,801
let's have one more toast.

242
00:20:52,361 --> 00:20:56,200
Ms. Ruan, happy Chinese New Year.

243
00:20:57,121 --> 00:20:58,920
Happy Chinese New Year.

244
00:21:07,166 --> 00:21:08,886
Mr. Fu.

245
00:21:08,886 --> 00:21:10,667
Thank you.

246
00:21:17,480 --> 00:21:23,480
[Li Zhi Huai: Ming Yu, happy Spring Festival.]

247
00:21:36,240 --> 00:21:39,081
Five minutes left.

248
00:21:39,081 --> 00:21:41,880
You're timing it?

249
00:21:43,323 --> 00:21:46,760
Four minutes and 30 seconds.

250
00:21:46,760 --> 00:21:49,880
Why does time go by so fast?

251
00:21:51,385 --> 00:21:54,080
Four minutes left.

252
00:21:54,080 --> 00:21:56,361
It flies by.

253
00:21:56,361 --> 00:21:59,281
I wish it would slow down.

254
00:22:01,997 --> 00:22:04,080
What happened to your cool image?

255
00:22:04,080 --> 00:22:06,800
I didn't know you were this clingy.

256
00:22:09,040 --> 00:22:11,360
What's wrong with being clingy?

257
00:22:13,220 --> 00:22:16,040
Fine. But you can't get too carried away.

258
00:22:16,040 --> 00:22:18,960
You have to leave soon.

259
00:22:18,960 --> 00:22:20,520
Don't want to leave.

260
00:22:20,520 --> 00:22:22,880
Don't want to go to work either.

261
00:22:22,880 --> 00:22:25,720
You're no different from a lovesick emperor.

262
00:22:25,720 --> 00:22:29,826
Don't make me the one who ruined your legacy.

263
00:22:29,826 --> 00:22:33,266
To be honest, it's getting a little annoying.

264
00:22:34,440 --> 00:22:36,000
You're annoyed with me?

265
00:22:36,000 --> 00:22:39,000
It's only been a few days,
and you're already annoyed?

266
00:22:39,000 --> 00:22:40,680
Don't you like me anymore?

267
00:22:40,680 --> 00:22:42,760
Didn't you say if I ever stopped liking you,

268
00:22:42,760 --> 00:22:44,801
I'd tell you straight up?
Would you even change?

269
00:22:44,801 --> 00:22:47,680
But how am I supposed to stop liking you?

270
00:22:49,361 --> 00:22:54,358
A vice president, pulling this act at home.

271
00:22:54,358 --> 00:22:57,680
Alright, fine. Hugs, cuddles.

272
00:22:59,668 --> 00:23:01,680
Time's up.

273
00:23:01,680 --> 00:23:03,121
Go to work.

274
00:23:03,121 --> 00:23:06,561
Hengshi Air needs you.
And I'm counting on you to pay my salary. Go.

275
00:23:06,561 --> 00:23:09,160
You're still counting down?

276
00:23:11,520 --> 00:23:13,600
Why are you back?

277
00:23:13,600 --> 00:23:15,680
Didn't finish the routine.

278
00:23:21,720 --> 00:23:23,801
Off to work!

279
00:23:23,801 --> 00:23:25,401
Refreshed.

280
00:23:25,401 --> 00:23:27,101
Bye.

281
00:23:28,081 --> 00:23:29,781
I'm off.

282
00:23:32,680 --> 00:23:34,720
Finally gone.

283
00:23:35,841 --> 00:23:37,680
I'm exhausted.

284
00:23:40,480 --> 00:23:43,640
Oh my gosh, he's not coming back, is he?

285
00:23:46,927 --> 00:23:49,760
Xuan, what are you doing here?

286
00:23:49,760 --> 00:23:53,280
I missed you. My mom had me
bring you some local specialties.

287
00:23:53,280 --> 00:23:59,760
You have no idea how much trouble it was
to get two boxes of red bean buns for you.

288
00:23:59,760 --> 00:24:02,040
What is it?

289
00:24:02,040 --> 00:24:04,561
- Isn't this Mr. Fu's phone?
- What?

290
00:24:04,561 --> 00:24:06,480
How'd it end up here?

291
00:24:07,270 --> 00:24:09,641
Yeah, it is.

292
00:24:09,641 --> 00:24:11,401
I'll give him a call.

293
00:24:11,401 --> 00:24:12,801
Sure, go ahead.

294
00:24:12,801 --> 00:24:15,401
I'll enjoy his ringtone.

295
00:24:15,401 --> 00:24:17,640
I'm calling Bai Yang.

296
00:24:21,040 --> 00:24:22,561
- Hello?
<i>- Babe.</i>

297
00:24:22,561 --> 00:24:24,881
<i>Did I leave my phone at home?</i>

298
00:24:24,881 --> 00:24:27,321
Yeah, on the couch.

299
00:24:27,321 --> 00:24:29,601
<i>Okay, I'll come pick it up.</i>

300
00:24:29,601 --> 00:24:32,280
No, I'm about to head out anyway.

301
00:24:32,280 --> 00:24:33,801
I'll drop it off for you.

302
00:24:33,801 --> 00:24:35,680
Just get to the office. Don't be late.

303
00:24:35,680 --> 00:24:37,940
<i>Okay, thanks.</i>

304
00:24:40,680 --> 00:24:42,400
I'm exhausted.

305
00:24:44,240 --> 00:24:46,921
- Did you drive?
- I did.

306
00:24:46,921 --> 00:24:48,361
I drove Xiao Zhen's car.

307
00:24:48,361 --> 00:24:52,200
Ever since she hit Mr. Fu's car last time,
she's been too scared to drive,

308
00:24:52,200 --> 00:24:56,121
so now it's basically my car.

309
00:24:58,680 --> 00:25:04,680
So, do you even know his phone password?

310
00:25:05,760 --> 00:25:08,000
What good is knowing that?

311
00:25:08,000 --> 00:25:10,520
I'd rather know his bank card's password.

312
00:25:10,520 --> 00:25:12,841
True. Good point.

313
00:25:12,841 --> 00:25:15,281
Alright, I'm going to get changed.

314
00:25:16,401 --> 00:25:18,160
He has a phone call.

315
00:25:23,841 --> 00:25:27,121
You should probably get that.
Might be something urgent.

316
00:25:33,561 --> 00:25:35,261
Hello?

317
00:25:37,960 --> 00:25:40,679
Who is this?

318
00:25:41,641 --> 00:25:43,680
<i>I'm looking for Fu Ming Yu.</i>

319
00:25:43,680 --> 00:25:45,841
<i>Is he not there?</i>

320
00:25:46,561 --> 00:25:49,361
He left his phone here.

321
00:25:49,361 --> 00:25:53,275
If it's urgent,
I'll have him call you back later.

322
00:25:53,275 --> 00:25:54,915
<i>It's not urgent.</i>

323
00:25:54,915 --> 00:25:58,401
I'm calling to thank him.

324
00:25:58,401 --> 00:26:00,761
The flowers he sent are beautiful.

325
00:26:17,480 --> 00:26:19,601
What's wrong? What are you thinking about?

326
00:26:19,601 --> 00:26:21,561
That call just now.

327
00:26:21,561 --> 00:26:23,801
It was a woman.

328
00:26:23,801 --> 00:26:25,641
So what? That's perfectly normal.

329
00:26:25,641 --> 00:26:27,481
You're not jealous over that, are you?

330
00:26:27,481 --> 00:26:33,082
She said thank you to Fu Ming Yu
for the beautiful flowers.

331
00:26:43,641 --> 00:26:45,440
Honestly, I don't think it's a big deal.

332
00:26:45,440 --> 00:26:47,161
People send flowers all the time.

333
00:26:47,161 --> 00:26:50,161
It could be a client or someone from work.

334
00:26:50,161 --> 00:26:51,162
Don't worry about it.

335
00:26:51,162 --> 00:26:53,440
Don't let it get to you.

336
00:26:53,440 --> 00:26:55,361
Then why are you speeding up?

337
00:26:55,361 --> 00:26:58,240
I don't think sending flowers is a big deal.

338
00:26:58,240 --> 00:26:59,760
It could just be a courtesy.

339
00:26:59,760 --> 00:27:02,000
But this lady's move is a little deliberate.

340
00:27:02,000 --> 00:27:03,401
She heard you pick up.

341
00:27:03,401 --> 00:27:06,440
Anyone with half a brain would know
that's his girlfriend answering,

342
00:27:06,440 --> 00:27:08,161
yet she still made a point of telling you.

343
00:27:08,161 --> 00:27:12,040
She's got his number.
Couldn't she call him later?

344
00:27:12,040 --> 00:27:14,801
That makes sense.

345
00:27:14,801 --> 00:27:17,440
Always sharp, Xuan.

346
00:27:17,440 --> 00:27:20,760
You need to spare some attention
for this woman.

347
00:27:20,760 --> 00:27:23,401
I can't be bothered to keep tabs on everyone.

348
00:27:23,401 --> 00:27:27,121
You can't keep a love rat any more than
you can hold sand in your hand.

349
00:27:27,121 --> 00:27:30,040
If he wants to stray,
there's no holding him back.

350
00:27:30,040 --> 00:27:32,281
All I can do is be in charge of myself.

351
00:27:45,680 --> 00:27:47,480
Morning, Si Xian.

352
00:27:47,480 --> 00:27:49,000
There was a call earlier.

353
00:27:49,000 --> 00:27:53,080
Some woman said
the flowers Mr. Fu sent were beautiful.

354
00:27:53,080 --> 00:27:55,840
You might want to have
Fu Ming Yu call her back.

355
00:27:57,927 --> 00:27:59,627
Wait...

356
00:28:00,921 --> 00:28:03,680
Was that a little tense just now?

357
00:28:06,760 --> 00:28:08,720
"There was a call earlier."

358
00:28:08,720 --> 00:28:12,320
"Some woman said
the flowers Mr. Fu sent were beautiful."

359
00:28:12,320 --> 00:28:16,560
"You might want to have
Fu Ming Yu call her back."

360
00:28:17,601 --> 00:28:21,361
- She said that exactly?
- Yes, that's all she said.

361
00:28:22,298 --> 00:28:24,561
Any jealousy in there?

362
00:28:24,561 --> 00:28:26,960
Let me do it again for you.

363
00:28:26,960 --> 00:28:28,480
"There was a call earlier."

364
00:28:28,480 --> 00:28:32,420
- "Some woman said the flowers Mr. Fu sent--"
- Alright, that's enough.

365
00:28:33,921 --> 00:28:37,680
Mr. Fu, if I may ask...

366
00:28:37,680 --> 00:28:41,480
Have you ever sent Ms. Ruan flowers?

367
00:28:41,480 --> 00:28:43,601
No. She said she doesn't like them.

368
00:28:43,601 --> 00:28:45,161
That's not how it works.

369
00:28:45,161 --> 00:28:48,280
She says she doesn't like it?
That's how you know she loves it.

370
00:28:48,280 --> 00:28:52,680
She says she doesn't like it,
but you still have to send it.

371
00:28:54,921 --> 00:28:57,121
We'll talk about it after work. Let's focus.

372
00:28:57,121 --> 00:28:58,920
You got this, boss.

373
00:29:00,040 --> 00:29:03,680
Was I just sitting in this chair?

374
00:29:14,561 --> 00:29:16,361
Do you have plans at home?

375
00:29:16,361 --> 00:29:17,641
Or want to come to my place?

376
00:29:17,641 --> 00:29:19,121
I don't want to go anywhere.

377
00:29:19,121 --> 00:29:20,841
Don't want to go home either.

378
00:29:20,841 --> 00:29:24,081
Okay then. Let's just wander around.

379
00:29:29,361 --> 00:29:30,880
Hello?

380
00:29:33,680 --> 00:29:36,480
Okay, got it.

381
00:29:39,280 --> 00:29:42,200
Well, guess I don't need
to figure out where to go.

382
00:29:42,200 --> 00:29:44,921
I'm on standby, and I just got called in.
Have to go pack.

383
00:29:44,921 --> 00:29:46,401
Where to?

384
00:29:46,401 --> 00:29:47,960
Jinhai City.

385
00:29:47,960 --> 00:29:50,420
Nice. A little change of scenery.

386
00:30:01,641 --> 00:30:03,841
Oh my.

387
00:30:03,841 --> 00:30:05,520
What's wrong?

388
00:30:05,520 --> 00:30:08,760
You know Li Zhi Huai, don't you?

389
00:30:08,760 --> 00:30:12,641
The name sounds familiar.
I think I've met her once or twice.

390
00:30:12,641 --> 00:30:16,440
I knew it. What did she want with you?

391
00:30:16,440 --> 00:30:19,841
Last time, she brought a film director
and a producer to see me.

392
00:30:19,841 --> 00:30:22,720
Said they wanted to make a biographical movie
based on me.

393
00:30:22,720 --> 00:30:24,161
Did you say yes?

394
00:30:24,161 --> 00:30:25,401
Of course not.

395
00:30:25,401 --> 00:30:26,841
What's there to film about me?

396
00:30:26,841 --> 00:30:28,361
Good thing you refused.

397
00:30:28,361 --> 00:30:31,401
She's such a media manipulator!

398
00:30:31,401 --> 00:30:34,401
She just announced she's making a movie
about a female pilot,

399
00:30:34,401 --> 00:30:36,440
and now she's involved in a scandal.

400
00:30:36,440 --> 00:30:39,480
And guess
who she's rumored to be involved with?

401
00:30:39,480 --> 00:30:41,519
Fu Ming Yu?

402
00:30:46,321 --> 00:30:48,960
Hey, you home yet?

403
00:30:49,561 --> 00:30:51,601
I've got a last-minute flight.

404
00:30:51,601 --> 00:30:53,040
What's wrong?

405
00:30:53,040 --> 00:30:55,000
Nothing. When are you back?

406
00:30:55,000 --> 00:30:56,401
Tomorrow.

407
00:30:56,401 --> 00:31:00,273
Alright. Text me when you land.

408
00:31:00,273 --> 00:31:01,973
Got it.

409
00:31:16,000 --> 00:31:19,960
Why has Ming Yu been so caught up
in drama lately?

410
00:31:19,960 --> 00:31:22,440
I wonder if Si Xian knows about this.

411
00:31:22,440 --> 00:31:23,601
Can she handle it?

412
00:31:23,601 --> 00:31:25,480
Si Xian?

413
00:31:26,121 --> 00:31:29,000
Ruan Si Xian, that female pilot.

414
00:31:29,000 --> 00:31:31,520
Isn't she Ming Yu's girlfriend?

415
00:31:31,520 --> 00:31:34,720
Well, maybe she still is, maybe not.

416
00:31:40,240 --> 00:31:42,400
[Jinhai City]

417
00:31:51,121 --> 00:31:54,200
Hello, welcome in. We have your table ready.

418
00:32:02,561 --> 00:32:05,501
- Would you like to order anything?
- Thank you.

419
00:32:11,361 --> 00:32:13,061
<i>Made it yet?</i>

420
00:32:13,960 --> 00:32:16,040
No, I forgot to reply.

421
00:32:16,040 --> 00:32:18,081
He's going to make a fuss again.

422
00:32:20,801 --> 00:32:23,561
<i>Made it, got a little busy just now.</i>

423
00:32:24,801 --> 00:32:26,501
<i>Okay.</i>

424
00:32:27,121 --> 00:32:28,720
What's this?

425
00:32:28,720 --> 00:32:31,761
Back to his factory settings?

426
00:32:37,321 --> 00:32:39,280
No follow-up?

427
00:32:39,280 --> 00:32:41,281
Nothing else?

428
00:32:42,480 --> 00:32:44,480
Sounds pretty confident.

429
00:32:44,480 --> 00:32:47,081
Maybe nothing is wrong?

430
00:32:54,979 --> 00:32:56,920
Look at this.

431
00:32:56,920 --> 00:33:01,840
"Made it, got a little busy just now."

432
00:33:01,840 --> 00:33:04,040
Eight words.

433
00:33:04,040 --> 00:33:06,081
Look at those eight words.

434
00:33:06,081 --> 00:33:07,960
She used two punctuation marks.

435
00:33:07,960 --> 00:33:11,561
A comma and a period.

436
00:33:13,200 --> 00:33:16,480
- So?
- There's a ton of information hidden in there.

437
00:33:16,480 --> 00:33:19,000
- Like what?
- Let me break it down for you.

438
00:33:19,000 --> 00:33:21,601
She landed at 4:10 p.m., right?

439
00:33:21,601 --> 00:33:25,641
What time is it now? 6:37 p.m. Beijing time.

440
00:33:25,641 --> 00:33:28,520
Think about it.
In the last two hours and 27 minutes,

441
00:33:28,520 --> 00:33:31,200
she said she was "a little busy."

442
00:33:32,040 --> 00:33:33,641
- Busy with what?
- What was she busy with?

443
00:33:33,641 --> 00:33:35,480
Exactly. A pilot lands, and that's it.

444
00:33:35,480 --> 00:33:36,841
She's off duty.

445
00:33:36,841 --> 00:33:38,480
- So what was she doing?
- What was she doing?

446
00:33:38,480 --> 00:33:41,361
- And who was she doing it with?
- Who was she with?

447
00:33:42,280 --> 00:33:47,040
Just spit it out! Stop with the suspense!

448
00:33:47,040 --> 00:33:49,041
Check the trending topics.

449
00:33:50,720 --> 00:33:52,401
Think about it.

450
00:33:52,401 --> 00:33:54,000
The last two hours

451
00:33:54,000 --> 00:33:57,520
were the most explosive hours
of this entire buzz.

452
00:33:57,520 --> 00:34:01,960
She must have been online, and by now
she's got the whole thing figured out.

453
00:34:04,801 --> 00:34:06,520
So you're saying

454
00:34:06,520 --> 00:34:08,801
she already knows about this?

455
00:34:08,801 --> 00:34:13,120
But she's pretending she doesn't
and acting completely calm.

456
00:34:13,120 --> 00:34:17,640
The calmest seas run the deepest.

457
00:34:21,921 --> 00:34:23,201
No.

458
00:34:23,201 --> 00:34:24,841
I'm going to call her.

459
00:34:24,841 --> 00:34:27,640
No, absolutely not.

460
00:34:28,480 --> 00:34:29,481
Think about it.

461
00:34:29,481 --> 00:34:32,960
You're in plain sight,
but she's in the shadows.

462
00:34:32,960 --> 00:34:35,080
You have no idea how much she knows.

463
00:34:35,080 --> 00:34:39,560
Didn't you say she knows everything?

464
00:34:39,560 --> 00:34:43,600
That was a guess. Merely a guess.

465
00:34:43,600 --> 00:34:46,640
And maybe she doesn't know anything.

466
00:34:46,640 --> 00:34:48,960
But that's unlikely, right?

467
00:34:48,960 --> 00:34:50,881
I mean, this thing is huge.

468
00:34:50,881 --> 00:34:53,121
Then what should I do now?

469
00:34:54,440 --> 00:34:56,521
Test the waters.

470
00:34:57,681 --> 00:34:59,281
Fish for clues.

471
00:34:59,281 --> 00:35:01,041
How?

472
00:35:01,041 --> 00:35:03,920
She said she was busy.

473
00:35:03,920 --> 00:35:07,080
Just ask her what she's busy with.

474
00:35:10,560 --> 00:35:12,520
Good one.

475
00:35:12,520 --> 00:35:16,080
- What are you doing?
- Yes, and throw in a little smiley face emoji.

476
00:35:16,080 --> 00:35:17,480
A cute one?

477
00:35:17,480 --> 00:35:19,241
No, too stiff.

478
00:35:19,241 --> 00:35:23,000
This one, the one with blush.

479
00:35:23,000 --> 00:35:24,600
- Blush?
- Girls like that.

480
00:35:24,600 --> 00:35:26,300
Okay.

481
00:35:27,080 --> 00:35:28,201
Sending it?

482
00:35:28,201 --> 00:35:29,901
Go for it.

483
00:35:33,201 --> 00:35:35,080
"Hang on, busy."

484
00:35:35,080 --> 00:35:36,780
With a period.

485
00:35:41,361 --> 00:35:42,881
So?

486
00:35:42,881 --> 00:35:44,921
She's in Jinhai City.

487
00:35:44,921 --> 00:35:47,840
What could she possibly be busy with?

488
00:35:52,401 --> 00:35:55,361
Do you know who's the first
to find Ruan Si Xian?

489
00:35:55,361 --> 00:35:57,120
Yan An.

490
00:35:57,120 --> 00:36:01,440
But that guy just couldn't stop showing off.

491
00:36:01,440 --> 00:36:03,801
He sent the video straight to Fu Ming Yu,

492
00:36:03,801 --> 00:36:06,480
and Fu Ming Yu went straight
to the Aviation Academy.

493
00:36:06,480 --> 00:36:11,681
I'll admit, Fu Ming Yu's looks
can be pretty deceiving,

494
00:36:11,681 --> 00:36:16,520
but honestly,
Si Xian's taste in men is not great.

495
00:36:16,520 --> 00:36:19,481
Yeah, not great.

496
00:36:21,080 --> 00:36:23,240
Si Xian!

497
00:36:23,921 --> 00:36:26,001
Are you eating here too?

498
00:36:27,801 --> 00:36:29,521
She's Si Xian.

499
00:36:30,216 --> 00:36:34,000
I heard this restaurant has a story.

500
00:36:34,000 --> 00:36:37,801
Didn't expect the one I'd walk into
would be my own.

501
00:36:37,801 --> 00:36:40,761
Si Xian, it's great to meet you here.

502
00:36:40,761 --> 00:36:44,000
Mom, I only know bits and pieces
of the things you asked.

503
00:36:44,000 --> 00:36:45,441
But now here's the real deal.

504
00:36:45,441 --> 00:36:46,481
- Si Xian, have a seat.
- Wait...

505
00:36:46,481 --> 00:36:49,721
Tell us firsthand.

506
00:36:49,721 --> 00:36:51,600
- Probably not a good idea.
- It's fine.

507
00:36:51,600 --> 00:36:53,481
Join us.

508
00:36:55,281 --> 00:36:56,361
My stuff--

509
00:36:56,361 --> 00:37:00,040
I'll get it. Excuse me, can we get
another set of utensils over here?

510
00:37:00,040 --> 00:37:01,520
It's perfect.

511
00:37:01,520 --> 00:37:02,881
And a glass, please.

512
00:37:02,881 --> 00:37:04,581
Sure.

513
00:37:07,520 --> 00:37:09,360
Here is your plate.

514
00:37:11,361 --> 00:37:13,281
Enjoy your meal.

515
00:37:13,281 --> 00:37:17,040
Your favorite Sweet-and-Sour Pork Ribs.

516
00:37:17,040 --> 00:37:18,800
Have some.

517
00:37:19,960 --> 00:37:21,681
- Thanks.
- Serve them on that table.

518
00:37:21,681 --> 00:37:24,520
- Sure. Please wait a moment.
- Together.

519
00:37:24,520 --> 00:37:26,361
Don't be so formal.

520
00:37:26,361 --> 00:37:29,681
Just say whatever comes to mind.

521
00:37:29,681 --> 00:37:31,600
I haven't introduced you yet, right?

522
00:37:31,600 --> 00:37:34,440
Mom, this is Ruan Si Xian.

523
00:37:34,440 --> 00:37:39,401
And this is my dearest mother,

524
00:37:39,401 --> 00:37:43,320
the renowned painter, Ms. Dong Xian.

525
00:37:45,640 --> 00:37:50,681
You both have a "Xian" in your names,
exactly the same character--

526
00:37:50,681 --> 00:37:54,601
You An, let "Captain" Ruan have her dinner.

527
00:37:56,241 --> 00:37:57,281
Right.

528
00:37:57,281 --> 00:37:59,840
These ribs are amazing.

529
00:37:59,840 --> 00:38:01,760
This one too.

530
00:38:09,721 --> 00:38:15,080
Si Xian, there's a question
I've been dying to ask.

531
00:38:15,080 --> 00:38:17,080
Go ahead.

532
00:38:17,080 --> 00:38:21,400
You came all the way to the beach by yourself
to unwind?

533
00:38:22,160 --> 00:38:25,801
So, how are you feeling?

534
00:38:25,801 --> 00:38:27,720
Pretty good.

535
00:38:32,120 --> 00:38:33,720
So-so?

536
00:38:34,440 --> 00:38:36,120
See, Mom? What did I tell you?

537
00:38:36,120 --> 00:38:38,321
Si Xian is a total boss.

538
00:38:38,321 --> 00:38:40,960
Unshakable.

539
00:38:40,960 --> 00:38:42,841
Except for that taste.

540
00:38:42,841 --> 00:38:44,520
That part is a little questionable.

541
00:38:44,520 --> 00:38:46,640
You An, that's enough.

542
00:38:46,640 --> 00:38:48,000
Don't bother her.

543
00:38:48,000 --> 00:38:49,480
You were so curious earlier.

544
00:38:49,480 --> 00:38:51,480
Now that she's here, but you're too shy to ask?

545
00:38:51,480 --> 00:38:53,281
Curious about what?

546
00:38:53,281 --> 00:38:55,240
My personal life?

547
00:38:59,640 --> 00:39:05,120
Si Xian, in my book, you are top-tier.

548
00:39:05,120 --> 00:39:08,480
Anyone else would have been
a total mess by now.

549
00:39:08,480 --> 00:39:12,401
But look at you. Eating, drinking,
not a care in the world.

550
00:39:12,401 --> 00:39:14,681
Why would I be a mess?

551
00:39:14,681 --> 00:39:18,560
Zheng You An, did you have something weird
in your drink today?

552
00:39:18,560 --> 00:39:19,921
Talking trash?

553
00:39:19,921 --> 00:39:21,721
I'm not talking trash!

554
00:39:21,721 --> 00:39:26,801
I genuinely admire you, I swear.

555
00:39:26,801 --> 00:39:31,401
Something this huge blows up online,
yet you're so calm.

556
00:39:31,401 --> 00:39:33,360
What huge thing?

557
00:39:35,841 --> 00:39:37,600
She doesn't know?

558
00:39:37,600 --> 00:39:39,640
Know what?

559
00:39:40,764 --> 00:39:43,480
- Mr. Fu.
- How's it going?

560
00:39:43,480 --> 00:39:45,160
We can't get the trending topic down.

561
00:39:45,160 --> 00:39:47,321
There's no other entertainment news
after the holiday,

562
00:39:47,321 --> 00:39:49,080
so netizens are latching onto this.

563
00:39:49,080 --> 00:39:52,560
They even dug up that you two
went to the same high school.

564
00:39:52,560 --> 00:39:53,921
But that was so long ago.

565
00:39:53,921 --> 00:39:56,441
Why is this coming out now?

566
00:40:00,640 --> 00:40:06,040
<i>If one day you fall for someone else
without telling me,</i>

567
00:40:06,040 --> 00:40:07,281
<i>I'll...</i>

568
00:40:07,281 --> 00:40:08,921
<i>You'll what?</i>

569
00:40:08,921 --> 00:40:10,960
<i>Send a funeral wreath to you.</i>

570
00:40:10,960 --> 00:40:14,200
<i>I'll put your memorial altar front and center.</i>

571
00:40:16,080 --> 00:40:22,080
No. This has to be resolved
before she gets back tomorrow.

572
00:40:23,600 --> 00:40:27,080
This is a little hot.

573
00:40:28,040 --> 00:40:30,721
<i>They look great together.
Very easy on the eyes.</i>

574
00:40:30,721 --> 00:40:35,120
<i>Leave Li Zhi Huai alone.
Focus on her work. And go away, scandals!</i>

575
00:40:35,120 --> 00:40:40,160
<i>She's going to play a female pilot, isn't she?
So dating an airline boss makes total sense.</i>

576
00:40:45,440 --> 00:40:48,720
It's obvious to anyone with eyes

577
00:40:48,720 --> 00:40:51,760
that this woman is just trying to make a scene.

578
00:40:51,760 --> 00:40:55,709
But to be fair, a wise man
doesn't stand under a crumbling wall.

579
00:40:55,709 --> 00:40:57,881
Fu Ming Yu handled this poorly too.

580
00:40:57,881 --> 00:40:59,201
He's not blameless.

581
00:40:59,201 --> 00:41:03,120
You An, we don't know the full story yet.
Don't jump to conclusions.

582
00:41:03,120 --> 00:41:04,721
Looks like we don't have enough food.

583
00:41:04,721 --> 00:41:06,600
Go grab a couple more dishes.

584
00:41:06,600 --> 00:41:07,721
Go on.

585
00:41:07,721 --> 00:41:10,560
Good idea.
I happen to know two amazing dishes here.

586
00:41:10,560 --> 00:41:12,520
I'll make an extra order.

587
00:41:12,520 --> 00:41:14,600
Si Xian, this is on me.

588
00:41:14,600 --> 00:41:15,801
Eat however much you want.

589
00:41:15,801 --> 00:41:17,601
My treat!

590
00:41:27,881 --> 00:41:30,520
You must be pretty pleased.

591
00:41:30,520 --> 00:41:32,961
You get a front-row seat to my drama.

592
00:41:37,841 --> 00:41:39,881
I am very pleased,

593
00:41:39,881 --> 00:41:43,321
because I have two wonderful daughters.

594
00:41:43,321 --> 00:41:48,080
It's so rare for us to sit down
and eat together like this.

595
00:41:48,080 --> 00:41:50,121
It makes me really happy.

596
00:41:51,201 --> 00:41:55,680
And if something else is on your mind,

597
00:41:55,680 --> 00:41:56,761
I'm sorry about that too.

598
00:41:56,761 --> 00:42:01,640
Weren't you going to talk to me?
Help me get to know Fu Ming Yu better?

599
00:42:05,080 --> 00:42:10,761
I thought about it,
and I realized I did overstep before.

600
00:42:10,761 --> 00:42:12,761
You're an adult now.

601
00:42:12,761 --> 00:42:15,000
You have your own judgment.

602
00:42:15,000 --> 00:42:16,881
As for my opinion?

603
00:42:16,881 --> 00:42:18,600
It doesn't matter that much.

604
00:42:18,600 --> 00:42:21,160
As long as you're happy, that's what counts.

605
00:42:21,160 --> 00:42:22,321
Isn't that how I've always lived?

606
00:42:22,321 --> 00:42:24,360
That is how you've always lived.

607
00:42:25,000 --> 00:42:28,560
When it comes to relationships, relax.

608
00:42:28,560 --> 00:42:32,960
I think the most important thing
is to enjoy the ride.

609
00:42:32,960 --> 00:42:35,321
The outcome isn't that important.

610
00:42:35,321 --> 00:42:39,280
So that's why you left Dad and me?

611
00:42:47,160 --> 00:42:48,881
Si Xian,

612
00:42:50,080 --> 00:42:56,001
I've always wanted to find the right time
to sit down and talk to you about this,

613
00:42:57,201 --> 00:42:59,041
but...

614
00:43:01,320 --> 00:43:04,120
[Fu Ming Yu]

615
00:43:06,600 --> 00:43:08,640
Hello?

616
00:43:08,640 --> 00:43:10,340
Hello?

617
00:43:13,321 --> 00:43:15,281
I'm going to clear something up with you.

618
00:43:15,281 --> 00:43:18,640
<i>Let's talk tomorrow.</i>

619
00:43:18,640 --> 00:43:22,800
In person. I need some quiet time today.

620
00:43:24,080 --> 00:43:25,780
Okay.

621
00:43:36,480 --> 00:43:38,241
No need to analyze anymore.

622
00:43:38,241 --> 00:43:40,200
She definitely knows.

623
00:43:41,160 --> 00:43:42,480
What do you mean?

624
00:43:42,480 --> 00:43:44,960
What did she say?

625
00:43:44,960 --> 00:43:47,589
She said we'll talk in person tomorrow.

